M10 objective delivery when a follow-up conversation is preempted.
Objectives 1001/1002/1004 (Power Plant, Con Yard, Comm Center destroyed) and
1005 (SE gate poked with key 1) are sent only from Action_Complete when the
non-key conversations M10CON014/005/011/002 end. ActiveConversationClass::
Start_Conversation stops a non-key conversation with INTERRUPTED at once if
any key conversation is active (23 M10 conversations are key). Retail called
Monitor_Conversation after Start_Conversation, so nothing observed that stop
and the primary was lost; Mission_Complete(true) then became unreachable.

Register the monitor before Start_Conversation. The immediate stop then
reaches the existing Action_Complete synchronously (reason INTERRUPTED; M10
never checks the reason) and the objective is sent at the moment of the kill
or poke. Without a key conversation, Start_Conversation never touches the
monitor array, so the conversation, its end and the objective timing are
unchanged. If Create_Conversation fails (id < 0), deliver directly. A saved
per-script flag (unused ids: Power Plant 2, Con Yard 1, Comm Center 1,
Gate_Check 4) makes each send happen once; old saves load it as false.
Engine conversation code is unchanged.

